const types={code:'Code / arithmetic',jev:'Jev judgement',prose:'Writing model',writer:'Writer choice'};
const scenarios=[
 {id:'steady',name:'Writing steadily',hint:'90 seconds of a steady run',badge:'Quiet by rule',description:'Default thresholds: a continuous run of at least 90 seconds, gaps at most 4 seconds, deletion share at most 30%, and active edits in at least 45% of its seconds.',steps:[['code','Read the edit rhythm','A one-second tick reads timings and edit counts. It proposes flow after sustained steady writing.','state'],['jev','Ask if this is composition','A Noul question asks whether this is forward composition that cards would interrupt. While waiting, the state stays settling.','flow-gate'],['code','Apply the confirmation threshold','An answer ≥ 0.40 accepts flow. Missing client, budget, or answer also accepts local flow. A lower answer holds settling for three minutes.','flow-gate'],['code','Hold ambient cards','The conductor sets data-flow. Full flow shows zero ordinary cards and dims the workspace; it does not toggle the manual Zen layout.','zen']],outcome:['The page becomes quiet.','Jev can veto entry, but a successful judgement is not required. Some other producers still run independently.']},
 {id:'rewrite',name:'Rewriting a sentence',hint:'Three versions of the same sentence',badge:'Independent tool path',description:'The struggle tracker uses paragraph history, not the conductor’s flow state. It checks after a 1.2-second pause, plus a separate 42-second stall check.',steps:[['code','Notice repeated rewriting','Three rewrites of one sentence create a Sentence Lab hint with strength 0.60. The overall struggle score must reach 0.50.','struggle'],['jev','Select a tool or leave it alone','Jev chooses Leave, Sentence Lab, Rhythm Strip, Claim Check, or Reader Questions. Low confidence marks tentative; it does not itself reject the choice.','tool-choice'],['code','Use the local fallback if needed','If judgement fails, the strongest local hint can open a tool when strength ≥ 0.60. The initial card is seeded by code.','tool-choice'],['prose','Fill the selected tool when possible','Sentence Lab can request up to three alternatives from the configured in-flow-tool model. Without a prose provider, it shows earlier attempts only.','generation']],outcome:['Sentence Lab can appear without Jev.','Its usefulness depends on the available attempts and a separately configured prose model. The proposed replacement gives alternatives clear purposes and meaning checks.']},
 {id:'stuck',name:'Pausing after heavy revision',hint:'65% deletion share, 20-second pause',badge:'State and help differ',description:'Assume the previous state was working and default timing thresholds apply. A pause alone does not establish that help is wanted.',steps:[['code','Classify the local state as stuck','A pause ≥ 18 seconds plus recent churn ≥ 0.40 is enough. The conductor does not pass in the richer paragraph struggle score.','state'],['jev','Ask whether to offer a way in','The unresolved-passage Noul must reach 0.60. A Choice picks from five fixed prompts, such as say it plainly or leave TK and move on.','way-in'],['code','Distinguish two unavailable cases','No Convex client permits a local template only at churn ≥ 0.60 and the learned stuck pause. A present client with a failed or skipped judgement does not get that fallback.','way-in'],['code','Choose the card by fixed precedence','An eligible way-in leads. Otherwise choose the best card overlapping this paragraph, then the top card overall. Include its linked items.','ranking']],outcome:['“Stuck” does not mean Jev approved an intervention.','Without a way-in, an existing ranked card can still surface. The current way-in supplies coaching templates, not alternative sentences.']},
 {id:'source',name:'A source becomes available',hint:'Research arrives beside the draft',badge:'Search + ordinary ranking',description:'Automatic research and source-card selection are separate steps. A result appearing beside a claim does not mean the claim has been verified.',steps:[['prose','Extract a research target','After the research debounce and gates, the configured research-extract model identifies claims, quotations, people, works, or other targets.','research'],['code','Search and order the results','A selected search backend retrieves results. Metadata completeness and input order contribute to ranking; this is not a Jev support verdict.','research'],['code','Ingest the bibliography arrival','The conductor makes a source item from the stored result. It does not add a new semantic confirmation for that arrival.','ingest'],['code','Apply attention and card score','Source base priority is 0.55; comment is 0.90. History, age, overlap, and relevance modify the scores. Full flow holds both.','ranking']],outcome:['A source card can arrive without a new Jev call.','A useful next version should show the exact supporting excerpt and whether it supports, narrows, or contradicts the draft claim.']},
 {id:'quick',name:'An issue marker appears',hint:'650 ms after a paragraph edit',badge:'Model choice, fixed copy',description:'Quick Review is installed alongside the other services. It requires an enabled, editable, visible editor, online state, a Convex client, and at least 80 characters in the paragraph.',steps:[['code','Schedule a paragraph check','The producer waits 650 ms, collects current passage, preceding text, goal, and audience, then uses cache and shared budget.','quick'],['jev','Choose one issue category','No clear issue, Needs context, Check evidence, Possible repetition, or Meaning is unclear.','quick'],['code','Attach a fixed explanation','The category indexes predefined copy. Low confidence adds “Possibly”. No clear issue gives no mark. A failed judgement does not create a heuristic issue.','quick'],['writer','Open or dismiss the mark','The writer reveals the popover. The explanation is a template, not a fresh paragraph-specific critique or generated rewrite.','quick']],outcome:['A model selected the category, not the wording.','This explains why a supposedly intelligent card can still feel generic.']},
 {id:'zen',name:'Choosing Zen yourself',hint:'A deliberate focus preference',badge:'No model required',description:'Manual Zen is a persisted editor preference. Automatic flow is a separate attention state with different effects.',steps:[['writer','Toggle manual Zen','Your explicit action changes the editor preference. No Jev or prose-model request is needed.','zen'],['code','Update the editor layout','The editor and route ignore source:flow for the manual Zen preference. A normal manual event controls the stored setting and panel layout.','zen'],['code','Hide the ambient flow surface','Manual Zen hides the flow surface. A high model relevance score cannot override that visibility gate.','visibility'],['writer','Return when you choose','An automatic-focus override exists, but it suppresses setFocus only. It does not prevent flow state or flow-based card suppression.','zen']],outcome:['You own manual Zen.','The “Automatic focus” switch currently disables the entire conductor, including cards, which is a broader effect than its label suggests.']}
