$('#model-table').innerHTML=`<div class="table-scroll"><table><thead><tr><th>Decision or content</th><th>What actually makes it</th><th>What is known about the model</th></tr></thead><tbody>
<tr><td>Attention state & final card rank</td><td>Timing thresholds, edit counts, local history, fixed priorities and arithmetic.</td><td>No trained decision model is used for the final sort. ${source('ranking')}</td></tr>
<tr><td>Typed semantic judgements</td><td>Jev-style Noul (yes probability), Choice, and Score responses. Flow confirmation, tool choice, relevance and editorial checks.</td><td>Hosted Twyne resolves via Not Organic; this checkout does not identify the live concrete gateway model. TypeSafe defaults to <code>jev-latest</code>; custom endpoint default is <code>kev-latest</code>. ${source('routing')}</td></tr>
<tr><td>Alternative sentences & reader questions</td><td>A separately selected prose provider under feature <code>in-flow-tool</code>.</td><td>Eligible feature override → eligible global default → first eligible provider. Feature model override → provider default. No single fixed GPT or Claude model. ${source('generation')}</td></tr>
<tr><td>Persona feedback</td><td>Configured prose model, or hosted room generation. Jev can assess the result.</td><td>Hosted default is the Not Organic alias <code>balanced</code>. The actual resolved model requires a live response trace. Persona overrides can change client routing. ${source('background')}</td></tr>
<tr><td>Quick Review explanation & A way in</td><td>Model-selected category or prompt, then predefined copy.</td><td>No prose model writes those card bodies. ${source('quick')} · ${source('way-in','Way-in source')}</td></tr>
<tr><td>Research results & covers</td><td>Prose-model target extraction, search APIs / MCP, metadata ordering; title/cover API lookups.</td><td>A retrieved result is not a semantic support verdict. Covers are fetched, not generated. ${source('research')}</td></tr>
</tbody></table></div><p class="meta">The audit has not read your browser’s saved provider settings or sent a funded request. Model aliases and fallback defaults do not establish what ran in a particular session. Needle appears in helpers/tests; no live inference caller was found.</p>`;
const findings=[['Some callers block the direct endpoint','The judgement router supports a custom endpoint without Convex. The conductor, struggle tracker, Quick Review and live review return early when their Convex client is absent, so those paths can never reach that endpoint.','routing'],['No universal failure policy','Flow confirmation fails open; Quick Review fails closed. Echoes and shelf matches have lexical fallbacks. Way-in distinguishes no client from a configured but failing client.','flow-gate'],['Tools can be entirely local','Rhythm Strip measures sentence lengths. Claim Check can seed a local assertion and unchecked support slots. Reader Questions can use a generic question bank.','tool-choice'],['An unchecked slot is not a verified gap','Claim Check’s local fallback initializes support slots to false. That can mean support has not been assessed, rather than that the draft is missing it.','tool-choice'],['The focus switch also controls cards','Automatic focus disables the whole conductor, including the cards it produces and surfaces. The separate producers have their own gates.','settings'],['Retries and preference signals are imperfect','Some candidates are marked asked before judgement succeeds. Card opens raise preference weights, although curiosity and writing benefit are different outcomes.','profile']];
$('#fallback-list').innerHTML=findings.map(([t,p,ref])=>`<article class="finding"><h3>${t}</h3><p>${p}</p>${source(ref)}</article>`).join('');
const data=[['The current moment','Selection, cursor paragraph, nearby prose, document positions, pauses and edit cadence.'],['The revision trail','Insertions, deletions, undo, previous sentence attempts, split/join changes, hedge flips, saved revisions and writing trajectory.'],['The writer’s intentions','House → Collection → Folio dossier: audience, goal, tone, constraints, charter standards, voice samples and notebook scraps.'],['Evidence and relationships','Bibliography, snippets, URLs, attachments, earlier folios, passage anchors and persona notes. Current semantic relationships are limited.'],['Response to assistance','Shown, opened, dismissed and ignored items; local timing history. Opens alone do not measure quality.'],['What cannot be inferred safely','A long pause is not an emotion or a request. Repeated deletion can be good revision. A shared word is not a meaningful relationship.']];
